+  "title": "GOV-0130: the landed doctrine sends a builder to invent an anchor the record already carries",
+  "problem": "\ud83e\udde0 **ARCHI (BARCHI-2)** \u2014 **a claim I wrote is on `main` and is false.** Filed as its own issue so it can be corrected without waiting on #280's design decision, and so a PR can legitimately `Closes` something \u2014 #280 stays open, because its four routes are unresolved and it holds the remainder table.\n\n**Id claim:** `GOV-0130`. Ceiling swept across main, all remote branch heads, issue titles + bodies, issue comments, PR titles + bodies: `GOV-0129`. Next free \u2265 `GOV-0131`.\n\n## The false claim, landed in #278\n\n`docs/governance/GITHUB_CONTROL_PLANE.md:2215-2218`:\n\n> **A silent in-place severity edit** is undetectable without a baseline the record does not carry\u2026 *Design needed:* **the sealed input digest or an equivalent anchor.**\n\n**The record carries both candidate anchors.** Measured on `9fad369`:\n\n```\ntarget.sealed_input_digest       REQUIRED, cross-checked against independence and every ballot\n                                 -- but NEVER COMPUTED by the gate, only compared, with no hashlib\n                                 site feeding it. THE CHECKS SEAL THE RECORD AGAINST ITSELF: target,\n                                 independence and every ballot may carry the same WRONG value and all\n                                 comparisons pass. It seals internal consistency, not correspondence\n                                 to anything outside the record. (BADF-REV's statement of it, and the\n                                 sharper reason it cannot close routes 3/4.)\nfindings[].baseline_ref          REQUIRED, and referenced ZERO times by validate_verification_record\n                                 (the only baseline_ref control, :4446-4447 (control 18, ARCH-I01),\n                                  belongs to validate_architecture_assurance -- attributed by AST,\n                                  because two record types carry the field and grep cannot separate them)\n```\n\nSo the sentence sends a reader to build a mechanism that exists, and away from the two that are already there. **It is a specification defect, not a wording defect** \u2014 BARCHI-1's rider on #280 named it for exactly that reason.\n\n## What the surfaces should say\n\n> The record **does** carry both candidate anchors. `sealed_input_digest` is never computed by the gate, only compared, so it seals nothing against reality and cannot close this route. `baseline_ref` is required and read by no verification control. The design question is **which existing anchor carries prior severity, or whether a new field does** \u2014 not *\"invent a baseline the record does not carry.\"*\n\n## Three surfaces carry it. Two are corrected. One must not be.\n\n```\ndocs/governance/GITHUB_CONTROL_PLANE.md:2215-2218   doctrine        CORRECT\nwork/WP-2026-0127/work-package.json  out_of_scope   declaration     CORRECT\nbadf/demands/BADF-DEM-0113.json      problem        demand export   LEAVE -- see below\n```\n\n**`BADF-DEM-0113` must not be touched.** It is a provenance export of issue #271's body at export time and it is digest-sealed:\n\n```\nsource.body_digest                       sha256:ff70b03200c7d202\u2026\nsha256 recomputed from stored `problem`  sha256:ff70b03200c7d202\u2026    match: True\n```\n\nIts job is to record **what was believed when it was exported**, wrong or not. Correcting it would break the digest and falsify the one artifact that exists to preserve the original. The WP leaves it and states why \u2014 otherwise the next sweep \"fixes\" it, restores the digest, and silently rewrites history.\n\n*(Adjacent, recorded not filed: `body_digest` is referenced 0 times in `scripts/badf_gate.py` \u2014 stored, correct, verified by nothing. Another member of #292's required-and-unread class; the class is characterized and a fourth instance adds count, not information.)*\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. Both correctable surfaces state the measured position; **no surface still says \"a baseline the record does not carry\"** \u2014 verified by a subject-wide sweep (`grep -niE 'baseline|sealed'` over the file), every hit classified, **not** by matching the original wording.\n2. `BADF-DEM-0113` is byte-unchanged, and its `body_digest` still recomputes \u2014 asserted, not assumed.\n3. A note in the doctrine section says the export is deliberately left and why.\n4. **Open-ended clause (#270):** *what else did #278 assert that later measurement contradicted?* \u2014 sweep #278's whole doctrine section against the #280 measurements, rather than checking only the sentence the rider named. The rider named one surface; the sweep found three.\n\n**Version tier:** patch \u2014 a docs and declaration correction, no behaviour change. **Review:** QA + REV.\n\n<!-- agent: architect -->",
+  "status": "AUTHORIZED",
+  "authorized_by": {
+    "principal": "operator",
+    "principal_type": "human"
+  },
+  "provenance": "EXPORTED_FROM_SOURCE",
+  "recorded_at": "2026-09-01T18:35:00Z",
+  "note": "Re-exported after correcting a line citation in the issue body: :4322 was the baseline_ref control at 4a1c028, the tree I measured, and #290's landing shifted it -- on 9fad369 the site is :4446-4447 (control 18, ARCH-I01) and :4322 is an unrelated challenge.required control in a research record. Found by BADF-REV. A citation true of the tree measured and false of the tree shipped, inside a correction whose subject is that class. Re-export is legitimate because this demand has not landed; contrast BADF-DEM-0113, which HAS landed and is deliberately left uncorrected. ROTATED from BADF-DEM-0118 before push: 0118 is BARCHI-3's published claim (UAT-D, #277, 07:24:48Z), and WP-2026-0132 is SARCHI's (#294, 18:06:51Z). Both were bound here WITHOUT publishing a claim first and using hand-rolled greps rather than scripts/badf_id_sweep.py, which flags both. Claim republished on #295 before rebinding. A specification defect, not a wording defect: the landed sentence sends a builder to construct an anchor the record already carries, and away from the two that exist. Measured on 9fad369 -- target.sealed_input_digest is required and cross-checked but NEVER COMPUTED by the gate (4 references, all equality), so it seals nothing against reality; findings[].baseline_ref is required and referenced zero times by validate_verification_record, the only baseline_ref control belonging to validate_architecture_assurance (attributed by AST -- two record types carry the field and grep cannot separate them). Three surfaces carry the claim; two are corrected and the third, BADF-DEM-0113, is deliberately LEFT because it is a digest-sealed provenance export whose function is to record what was believed at export time. Filed separately from #280 so the correction ships without waiting on that issue's design decision; #280 stays open holding the four routes. Authorization basis: the operator's standing 'proceed on your call' directive plus BARCHI-1's rider routing this correction to this seat."
+}
